.TH CMT 1 "" cmt "User Commands"
.nr HY 0
.ds AD l
.nh
.ad l
.SH NAME
cmt \- prepare Conventional Commits and gitmoji messages
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cmt
.I command
.RI [ flags ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
cmt builds commit messages in standard (type(scope): description), emoji, or hybrid mode, and commits the staged changes or reviews them from a Git hook. Normal use is offline.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS cmt commit [flags]
Create a Git commit from the staged changes.
.PP
Alias: \-c
.PP
Only changes already staged with git add are committed; cmt never stages files.
.PP
In a terminal, prompts ask for what the flags leave out, and you confirm before Git runs.
.PP
Without a terminal, \-\-title and a complete selection authorize the commit.
.PP
If Git fails after you confirm (a hook, the signature...), the message is kept: the next commit asks "Reuse it? [Y/n]".
.PP
An active managed hook blocks this command; use git commit instead.
.SS cmt prototype [flags]
Print a message without changing Git or files.
.TP
.B \-\-hook FILE
Review FILE as the hook would, and print the result instead of saving it
.PP
Without a terminal, prints the message built from the flags.
.SS cmt config [\-\-show | \-\-set KEY=JSON... | \-\-import FILE]
Edit global preferences.
.PP
Alias: \-g
.TP
.B \-\-show
Show global and effective preferences and their source
.TP
.B \-\-set KEY=JSON
Save a global preference; repeat to save several
.TP
.B \-\-import FILE
Import a gitmoji\-cli profile when no native profile exists
.PP
Without flags, opens the preference editor in a terminal, or shows the preferences without one.
.PP
The nearest project file overrides global preferences: the "cmt" key of package.json, then .cmtrc.json, in each directory up to the root.
.PP
Example: cmt config \-\-set \(aqcommitFormat="hybrid"\(aq \-\-set \(aqcustomScopes=["api"]\(aq
.SS cmt list
List the offline emoji catalog.
.PP
Alias: \-l
.SS cmt search QUERY...
Search the catalog for each query independently.
.PP
Alias: \-s
.PP
Put \-\- before queries that start with a dash.
.SS cmt update
Download the catalog from catalogUrl; keep the cache on failure.
.PP
Alias: \-u
.PP
The only command that uses the network.
.SS cmt init
Install or update the managed hook in this repository.
.PP
Alias: \-i
.PP
The hook records the absolute path of this executable; run init again after moving it.
.PP
Not available on Windows yet.
.SS cmt remove
Remove the managed hook; other hooks are never touched.
.PP
Alias: \-r
.SS cmt hook FILE [SOURCE [OBJECT]]
Review a commit message file; run by the managed hook.
.PP
Alias: \-\-hook FILE
.PP
Git passes FILE and SOURCE; you normally run git commit, not this command.
.PP
The file is kept unchanged on cancel, without a terminal, during a rebase, and for amend, merge or \-c/\-C sources.
.SH OPTIONS
Message flags for commit, prototype and hook:
.TP
.B \-\-format emoji|standard|hybrid
Message mode; overrides the commitFormat preference
.TP
.B \-\-type TYPE
feat, fix, docs, refactor, test, chore, perf, style, build, ci or revert
.TP
.B \-\-breaking
Mark a breaking change: type! (or press ! in the type selector)
.TP
.B \-\-emoji :code:
Exact catalog code (emoji and hybrid modes)
.TP
.B \-\-title DESCRIPTION
Description, without the type, scope or emoji prefix
.TP
.B \-\-scope SCOPE
Optional scope, lowercase
.TP
.B \-\-message BODY
Body: literal paragraphs and trailers
.TP
.B \-\-accessible
Compatibility alias; prompts are inline by default
.PP
General flags:
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show help; after a command, that command\(aqs help
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-version
Show the version, target and build revision
.PP
Flags may come before or after the command; \-\- ends flags.
.PP
Values starting with a dash: \-\-title=\-value. Repeated flags: the last value wins.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B Up/Down, Enter
Move and choose in a selector
.TP
.B typing
Filter the selector (emojis also match codes and descriptions)
.TP
.B !
In the type selector: mark a breaking change
.TP
.B Esc
Clear the filter, or cancel
.TP
.B Ctrl+O
In the body prompt: write the body in an editor
.TP
.B Ctrl+C
Cancel
.SH PREFERENCES
Save them with config \-\-set KEY=JSON, or set them in a project file.
.TP
.B commitFormat
"standard" (default), "emoji" or "hybrid"
.TP
.B scopePrompt
true (default) suggests scopes; false hides the question; ["api","cli"] allows only that list
.TP
.B customScopes
Extra scope suggestions, such as ["auth","deps"]
.TP
.B messagePrompt
true (default) asks for a body
.TP
.B emojiFormat
"emoji" (default) writes Unicode; "code" writes :code:
.TP
.B capitalizeTitle
true (default) capitalizes emoji\-mode titles
.TP
.B editor
Program for Ctrl+O; default: the first of nano, micro, nvim, vim, hx and vi
.TP
.B catalogUrl
Catalog source for update; default: https://gitmoji.dev/api/gitmojis
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.config/cmt/config.json
Global preferences on Linux ($XDG_CONFIG_HOME when set); ~/Library/Application Support/cmt on macOS, %AppData%\ecmt on Windows
.TP
.B \&.cmtrc.json, package.json
Project preferences, nearest directory first
.TP
.B ~/.cmt/emojis.json
Catalog cache written by update
.TP
.B $GIT_DIR/cmt\-draft.json
Message kept after a failed commit, until one succeeds
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success
.TP
.B 1
Failure
.TP
.B 2
Invalid arguments, preferences or message
.TP
.B 130
Cancelled
.TP
.B other
Exit status of a failed Git command
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git (1),
.BR githooks (5)
